  "bundle": [
    {
      "path": "cordis.patch.yml",
      "text": "# dsh-tavily-pool bundle patch: mount the plugin and pin both providers.\n#\n# ⚠️ `config` on an id-targeted patch REPLACES the whole config object\n# (`cordis-plugin-include`'s `applyEntryPatches` does `target[key] = value` for\n# every key of the patch, so assigning `config` discards the previous one\n# entirely). Both provider fields must therefore be written out together:\n# omitting one drops it from the composed row, silently reverting that\n# capability to auto-selection instead of erroring. This is the exact mistake\n# `dsh-tavily@0.3.1` shipped. Verified by running the host's own\n# `applyEntryPatches` against the base row, and by `dsh --profile <p>\n# --dump-config`: a patch writing only `searchProvider` loses `fetchProvider`.\n#\n# Both fields point at the single provider id `tavily`: the seam keeps search and\n# fetch in two registries, and this plugin registers into both (ticket 01 for\n# search, ticket 10 for fetch). Pinning an id that is not registered makes every\n# call throw `WEB_PROVIDER_CONFIGURED_MISSING` — so a half-loaded plugin is a\n# broken one, which is why `apply()` registers both providers before anything\n# that can fail.\n#\n# To roll back by hand, point either field back at the official provider and keep\n# BOTH lines present:\n#   searchProvider: deepseek-official\n#   fetchProvider: http\n# See docs/usage.md (\"Manual rollback\").\n\n- insert:\n    - id: tavily-pool\n      name: dsh-tavily-pool\n\n- id: web\n  config:\n    searchProvider: tavily\n    fetchProvider: tavily\n"
    }
  ],
